## 6. Component Descriptions

| Component | Function |
|---|---|
| Arduino Uno | Executes the monitoring and alarm logic |
| Flame sensor | Detects IR radiation typical of flames; fast; needs line of sight; affected by sunlight and lamps |
| MQ-2 | Heated SnO2 gas sensor responding to smoke/combustible gases; needs warm-up and calibration; cross-sensitive to alcohol, humidity, and cooking vapors |
| Buzzer + NPN | Audible alarm without overloading the GPIO |
| Red LED | Warning / alarm |
| Green LED | Normal status |
| Amber LED | Simulated suppression indicator |
| Reset button | Manual acknowledgement/reset |

### Why an MQ-2 module is not a certified smoke detector
It is a general gas sensor, not a tested smoke detector. It is cross-sensitive, drifts with age, temperature, and humidity, has no self-test or standards approval, and its readings are only meaningful after warm-up and calibration against a clean-air baseline.

